# Clarifying questions (selectable UI only)

When requirements are ambiguous, under-specified, or have multiple valid approaches, **do not** close with open-ended, prose-only questions (“Which do you prefer?” with no UI). **Never** fall back to lettered Markdown (`1A`, `A/B/C`) or “reply with the option title”.

1. **Use the native selectable question tool** so the user gets clickable choices:
   - Grok Build: `ask_user_question`
   - Cursor: `AskQuestion`
2. Each option needs a short human **`label`** (Cursor also wants a stable **`id`**). Use **`allow_multiple` / `multi_select`** only when more than one answer can apply.
3. Prefer **several focused questions** over one long mixed list. Put the recommended option first and mark it `(Recommended)`.
4. If free-form input might still be needed, include **“Other — I’ll reply in chat”** as a last choice — do not rely on that as the only path.
5. If the tool errors, **retry it**. If it is still unavailable, say so in one sentence and stop. Do not invent a Markdown quiz.
